# Day for night: a scene shot in daylight graded to read as moonlight. Moonlight is the sun at about 1/400 000 of
# the brightness, so the eye sees it with little colour (rod vision) and a blue cast. A colourist sells it with
# exposure, colour and above all a dark sky: a bright sky is the giveaway.
#   under         the whole picture nearly two stops down
#   moon          a cool balance: blue, a hint of green taken out
#   sky           the sky far darker still, under a graduated window, so the land is the brightest part of the frame
#   sky_key       ... and its blue darkened through a hue key gated by the same graduated window (and), so bright
#                 ground is never touched; clip_white firms up the key
#   night_eyes    colour drains with the light: much less saturation, and least in the shadows (lum_vs_sat)
#   green_down    foliage is the other giveaway in daylight footage: greens calmer still
#   toe           soft shadows that still keep detail; a night grade dies if the blacks crush
#   edges         a heavier vignette, as if the moon only lights the middle of the frame
# Use it on daylight exteriors shot for night (hard back light and no sky in shot make it far easier).
cierra 0.1
name "day for night"
about "Nearly two stops under, moonlight blue, a very dark sky, colour drained by the dark, a heavy vignette."
input aces2065_1
output aces2(display: rec1886)

node under = exposure(stops: -1.7)
  label "nearly two stops under"
node moon = white_balance(temperature: -0.55, tint: 0.06)
  label "moonlight: cool, a hint of magenta to kill green"
node sky = exposure(stops: -1)
  label "a dark sky (the giveaway)"
  mask graduated(centre: [0.5, 0.55], angle: 90, falloff: [0.12, 0.3])
node sky_key = hue_vs_lum(points: [[345, -0.06, 50]])
  label "blue of the sky down further"
  mask graduated(centre: [0.5, 0.6], angle: 90, falloff: [0.1, 0.2]) and qualifier(hue: 290..30, sat: 0.008..1, clip_white: 0.8)
node night_eyes = lum_vs_sat(points: [[0.1, 0.25], [0.3, 0.45], [0.5, 0.6], [0.8, 0.55]])
  label "rod vision: colour drains in the dark"
node green_down = hue_vs_sat(points: [[206, 0.6, 40]])
  label "foliage calmer"
node toe = curve(points: [[0.0729, 0.0729], [0.15, 0.16], [0.3, 0.3], [0.5, 0.49], [1, 0.9]])
  label "shadow detail kept, highlights held under white"
node edges = vignette(amount: 0.3, softness: 0.8)

graph under -> moon -> sky -> sky_key -> night_eyes -> green_down -> toe -> edges
